  "rationale": [
    "the corrected VNP observation remains the radiometric authority",
    "water-specific weighting imposes an origin assumption not established by the observation",
    "Gate 2 found material and proxy-dependent shoreline redistribution",
    "similar ambiguity exists at other low-proxy boundaries",
    "no independent high-resolution nighttime reference currently establishes that water weighting improves allocation accuracy"
  ],
  "interpretation": "No-water-prior is the simplest structural allocation and the reporting primary. Water-weighted variants remain sensitivity analyses and negative controls.",
